# Licensure and Credentialing Policy
**Daisy Health**
**Policy ID:** HR-LC-009
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Last Reviewed:** June 1, 2025
**Owner:** Credentialing and Compliance

---

## Purpose

Daisy Health is a licensed virtual primary care provider. All clinical staff must hold current, active, and unrestricted professional licenses to practice. This policy outlines licensure requirements, the credentialing process, and how Daisy Health supports clinical employees in maintaining their credentials.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all clinical employees including physicians (MDs, DOs), nurse practitioners (NPs), physician assistants (PAs), registered nurses (RNs), clinical pharmacists (PharmDs), and behavioral health counselors (LCSWs, LPCs, psychologists).

Non-clinical employees are not subject to this policy.

---

## 1. Licensure Requirements

### Active License Required Before Starting

All clinical staff must hold an **active, unrestricted professional license** in at least one U.S. state before their first day of patient care. A license that is expired, suspended, or under investigation is not acceptable.

Clinical employees may not see patients until written confirmation of licensure verification is received from the Credentialing team.

### Multi-State Licensure

Daisy Health serves patients across multiple states. Clinical staff are expected to hold licensure in the states where they will serve patients. Daisy Health will support multi-state licensure as follows:

- **Compact licensure programs** (IMLC for physicians, NLC for nurses, APRN Compact where available) are the preferred path to multi-state practice. Daisy Health will cover compact licensure fees.
- For states not covered by compact licensure, Daisy Health will reimburse the cost of obtaining an additional state license (see Section 5).
- Clinical staff must disclose all current licenses and any disciplinary history to the Credentialing team during onboarding and upon any change.

### License in State of Physical Work Location

If a clinical employee works remotely from a state different from where their patients are located, they may also need a license in their physical work state, depending on that state's requirements. The Credentialing team will advise on a case-by-case basis. Employees should notify Credentialing before relocating, even temporarily.

---

## 2. The Credentialing Process

Credentialing is the process of verifying a clinician's qualifications, training, licensure, and background before they are authorized to practice under Daisy Health's agreements with health plans and facilities.

### Initial Credentialing

Upon hire, all clinical staff undergo initial credentialing, which includes:

- Verification of professional license(s) with the relevant state medical or licensing board
- Verification of education and training (medical school, residency, fellowship, pharmacy school, etc.)
- National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB) query
- Background check (criminal history, sex offender registry, OIG exclusion list)
- Verification of malpractice insurance history and any claims
- DEA registration verification (for prescribers)
- Verification of board certification (if applicable)

Initial credentialing typically takes **5–10 business days** for employed staff. Health plan credentialing (required for billing) takes **60–120 days** and is initiated simultaneously.

### Health Plan Credentialing

For clinical staff who bill insurance, credentialing with Daisy Health's health plan partners is required separately. During the health plan credentialing period:

- You may see patients and document care
- Daisy Health may not be able to bill for your services under your individual NPI until credentialing is complete
- You will be notified by the Credentialing team when health plan credentialing is finalized for each payer

### Recredentialing

Daisy Health conducts **recredentialing every 3 years** for all clinical staff, or more frequently if required by a health plan or regulatory body. Recredentialing involves updated verification of license status, absence of sanctions, malpractice history, and performance review.

---

## 3. License Maintenance and Renewal

Clinical employees are responsible for maintaining their licenses in good standing. This includes:

- Renewing licenses before expiration
- Completing all required continuing education (CE) or continuing medical education (CME) hours for renewal
- Notifying the Credentialing team of any license renewal, new license, or change in license status within **5 business days**
- Immediately notifying the Credentialing team if a license is placed under investigation, suspended, or restricted in any way

### Renewal Reminders

The Credentialing team tracks license expiration dates and will send a reminder **90 days before expiration**. It is ultimately the employee's responsibility to renew on time. An expired license results in **immediate suspension of patient care privileges** until the license is renewed and verified.

---

## 4. Continuing Education Requirements

| Role | CE/CME Requirement | Renewal Cycle |
|---|---|---|
| Physicians (MD/DO) | 50 CME hours | 2 years (varies by state) |
| Nurse Practitioners | 75 CE hours | 2 years |
| Physician Assistants | 100 CME hours | 2 years |
| Registered Nurses | 30 CE hours | 2 years (varies by state) |
| Clinical Pharmacists (PharmD) | 30 CE hours | 2 years |
| Behavioral Health Counselors | 40 CE hours | 2 years (varies by state) |

Daisy Health's **$1,000 professional development stipend** (see Expense Reimbursement Policy HR-EX-004) may be used toward CE/CME courses, conference attendance, and board exam fees.

---

## 5. Licensure Fee Reimbursement

Daisy Health reimburses the following licensure-related fees:

| Fee Type | Reimbursement |
|---|---|
| State license renewal (primary state) | Up to $300 per renewal cycle |
| Additional state license (required for patient care) | Up to $500 per new license |
| Compact licensure fees (IMLC, NLC) | Fully reimbursed |
| DEA registration | Fully reimbursed for applicable roles |
| Board certification exam | Up to $500 per exam, once per year |
| Board recertification | Up to $500 per cycle |

Reimbursement requires a receipt and proof of payment. Submit through the Expense Portal (see HR-EX-004).

---

## 6. Malpractice Insurance

Daisy Health provides **professional liability (malpractice) insurance** for all clinical staff for services performed within the scope of their employment at Daisy Health. This coverage:

- Applies to telehealth encounters conducted through the Daisy Health platform
- Is an occurrence-based policy
- Covers the states where Daisy Health is licensed to operate

Clinical employees are responsible for confirming that malpractice coverage extends to any state where they are physically working, particularly for temporary relocations. Contact the Credentialing team for confirmation before working from a new state.

Employees who conduct clinical activities outside the scope of Daisy Health employment (e.g., moonlighting, volunteer work) are responsible for their own malpractice coverage for those activities.

---

## 7. Reportable Events

Clinical employees must immediately notify the Credentialing team if any of the following occur:

- License suspension, restriction, probation, or revocation in any state
- DEA registration suspended or revoked
- Malpractice claim filed or settled
- Criminal charge or conviction of any kind
- Sanction or exclusion from any federal or state healthcare program (e.g., Medicare, Medicaid)
- Adverse action by any hospital, health plan, or licensing board

Failure to report these events may result in termination and referral to the appropriate licensing board.

---

## 8. DEA Registration

Prescribers (physicians, NPs, PAs with prescriptive authority, clinical pharmacists with prescriptive authority) must hold a valid DEA registration. Daisy Health:

- Reimburses DEA registration fees in full
- Requires DEA registration in the states where patients receive prescriptions, per DEA requirements
- Tracks DEA expiration dates and sends renewal reminders 90 days in advance

